  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have an n×nn \\times nn×n matrix aaa. You can rearrange the elements of the matrix in any way. Let m1,m2,…,mnm_1, m_2, \\dots, m_nm1​,m2​,…,mn​ be the medians of each row in aaa after the rearrangement. The goodness of the matrix aaa is defined as the minimum median among the medians of all rows i.e min⁡(m1,m2,…,mn)\\min(m_1, m_2, \\dots, m_n)min(m1​,m2​,…,mn​). Naturally, rearranging values also comes with a cost. The cost of rearrangement is defined as m1+m2+⋯+mnm_1 + m_2 + \\dots + m_nm1​+m2​+⋯+mn​.\n\nFind the **maximum goodness** you can achieve after rearranging a matrix aaa such that the cost of rearrangement doesn't exceed kkk or −1-1−1 if the answer doesn't exist.\n\nThe median of an array aaa consisting of nnn elements is the ⌈n+12⌉th\\lceil{\\frac{n+1}{2}}\\rceil^{th}⌈2n+1​⌉th smallest element of aaa. The median of [4,8,6,1][4, 8, 6, 1][4,8,6,1] is 666 and the median of [1,6,2,4,5][1, 6, 2, 4, 5][1,6,2,4,5] is 444.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer ttt denoting the number of test cases. The description of ttt test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case consists of two space-separated integers nnn and kkk.\nnnn lines follow, each consisting of nnn space-separated integers denoting the matrix aaa\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer - the maximum goodness you can achieve such that the rearrangement cost does not exceed kkk or `-1` if the answer doesn't exist.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤t≤1001 \\leq t \\leq 1001≤t≤100",
      "1≤n≤10001 \\leq n \\leq 10001≤n≤1000",
      "1≤k≤10141 \\leq k \\leq 10^{14}1≤k≤1014",
      "1≤ai,j≤1091 \\leq a_{i, j} \\leq 10^91≤ai,j​≤109",
      "1≤∑n≤10001 \\leq \\sum n \\leq 10001≤∑n≤1000",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (20 points):** k=1014k = 10^{14}k=1014",
      "**Subtask 2 (40 points):** 1≤∑n≤701 \\leq \\sum n \\leq 701≤∑n≤70",
      "**Subtask 3 (40 points):** Original constraints"
    ],
