        "output": "9\n6\n-1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:  We rearrange the matrix as follows:\n[11211617313351562432989]\\begin{bmatrix}\n11 & 2 & 1 & 16\\\\\n17 & 3 & 13 & 3\\\\\n5 & 15 & 6 & 24\\\\\n32& 9 & 8 & 9\n\\end{bmatrix}​1117532​23159​11368​163249​​\n. The medians of each row are 11,13,15,911, 13, 15, 911,13,15,9 respectively. The goodness is 999 and the cost is 484848. There are other rearrangements that may yield the same goodness but 999 is the maximum goodness we can get.\nTest case 222:  The rearranged matrix is:\n[17383216161132151352499]\\begin{bmatrix}\n17 & 3 & 8 & 3\\\\\n2 & 1 & 6 & 16\\\\\n11& 32 & 15 & 13\\\\\n5 & 24 & 9 & 9\n\\end{bmatrix}​172115​313224​86159​316139​​\n. The medians of each row are 8,6,15,98, 6, 15, 98,6,15,9 respectively. The goodness is 666 and the cost is 383838. There are other rearrangements that may yield the same goodness but 666 is the maximum goodness we can get.\nTest case 333:  No matter how we rearrange the elements, the cost is always greater than kkk."
